                <pb facs="0135" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg23"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7661/1.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Beaupré to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-07-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 19,
                    1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Beaupré states that the Government’s analysis of deviled ham shows a small
                    quantity of boric acid, and that time has been granted for reshipment until an
                    investigation has been made. Says he will send samples.)</p>
            </div>
